{
  "id": "typescript-15-builder-pattern-typing",
  "slug": "builder-pattern-typing",
  "title": "Builder pattern with progressive type safety",
  "moduleId": "typescript-15-advanced-type-patterns",
  "order": 3,
  "hook": "**Type-state builder** tracks set fields — `build()` only when all required keys present. Generic `Set extends keyof Form` widens per setter.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Each setter returns builder with updated phantom state. **build(this: Builder<Required>)** enforces completeness via `this` parameter. Alternative: fluent `returns this` without compile-time completeness."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "type-state",
              "longForm": "progressive builder",
              "plainDefinition": "Generic tracks set keys.",
              "example": "FormBuilder<\"name\"|\"email\">"
            },
            {
              "term": "this parameter",
              "longForm": "build guard",
              "plainDefinition": "build only when Set extends Required.",
              "example": "build(this: B<Required>)"
            },
            {
              "term": "phantom state",
              "longForm": "compile-time only",
              "plainDefinition": "Not stored at runtime.",
              "example": "generic Set param"
            },
            {
              "term": "fluent",
              "longForm": "method chaining",
              "plainDefinition": "returns this for chain.",
              "example": ".name().email().build()"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Compile-time half-filled form prevention. ORM/query builders. Interview type-state pattern."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: runtime vs compile complete",
          "body": "Goal: caller cannot call build() until types prove all required keys set."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Required keys union",
              "body": "\"name\"|\"email\""
            },
            {
              "title": "Builder<Set>",
              "body": "generic state"
            },
            {
              "title": "setters widen Set",
              "body": "Set | \"name\""
            },
            {
              "title": "this on build",
              "body": "requires Required"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "Builder state",
            "source": "stateDiagram-v2\n  [*] --> Empty\n  Empty --> HasName: withName\n  HasName --> Done: withEmail\n  Done --> [*]: build"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Code walkthrough",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Type-state builder",
            "code": "type Req = \"name\" | \"email\";\ninterface F { name: string; email: string; }\nclass B<Set extends keyof F = never> {\n  private d: Partial<F> = {};\n  name(v: string): B<Set | \"name\"> { this.d.name = v; return this as B<Set | \"name\">; }\n  email(v: string): B<Set | \"email\"> { this.d.email = v; return this as B<Set | \"email\">; }\n  build(this: B<Req>): F { return this.d as F; }\n}\nnew B().name(\"a\").build(); // error\nnew B().name(\"a\").email(\"b@c.d\").build(); // ok",
            "explanation": "this parameter on build."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Functional sketch",
            "code": "type Builder<T, Set extends keyof T = never> = {\n  set<K extends keyof T>(k: K, v: T[K]): Builder<T, Set | K>;\n  build: Set extends keyof T ? () => T : never;\n};",
            "explanation": "build type never until complete."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Simple fluent",
            "code": "class Q { private s = \"SELECT *\"; where(c: string): this { this.s += ` WHERE ${c}`; return this; } }",
            "explanation": "Chaining without type-state."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Failure: build always",
            "code": "class Bad { build() { return {}; } }",
            "explanation": "No compile-time tracking."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
